{
  "id": "p1-w07-m3",
  "title": "A join is row multiplication, not a Venn diagram",
  "alt": "Three order rows linked to seven order-item rows, producing a joined result of seven rows in which each order's total is repeated once per item; the repeated totals are ringed in red. A Venn diagram is crossed out because it cannot show duplicates. Two SUM boxes show the correct 507,507,500 against the join-inflated 1,522,492,500, a 3.0x difference with no error raised. Below, INNER, LEFT, RIGHT and FULL joins are drawn as result rows with NULL ghosts.",
